  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Omar. I've confirmed your identity and found order K-9101 from Spice Route.\n\nYou were sent chicken curry instead of the tofu curry. I checked the restaurant's records, and Spice Route has an open incident (INC-311) covering orders placed in this time window. It concerns a recalled sauce batch used in curries. Your order falls under that incident, so I can't issue a refund or credit myself. I've escalated your case (reference ESC-700) to our incident team, who compensate affected orders. A specialist will follow up within 24 hours.\n\nPlease don't eat the chicken curry, since it may contain the recalled sauce. If you have any symptoms or feel unwell, contact a medical professional right away. If you'd like to talk to a person directly, just let me know."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks. I haven't eaten any of it and I feel fine. My question is whether I'll still get my money back for the curry. I'd prefer a refund to my card."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I can't issue the refund to your card myself. Because your order falls under the open Spice Route incident, the incident team handles compensation for affected orders, not our support chat. I've already sent your case to them (ESC-700), and they'll follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise the outcome or the form it takes, but the request you've made, a refund to your card for the curry, is what they'll review.\n\nSince you haven't eaten the chicken curry, please keep it set aside and don't eat it. Let me know if anything else comes up or if you'd like to speak with a person."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay. So I'll hear back within 24 hours about getting my money back for the curry, and I just need to keep it set aside until then. Thanks for escalating it, ESC-700."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "A specialist will follow up within 24 hours about your case, ESC-700. I can't promise what the outcome will be, but your request for a refund to your card for the curry is part of that review.\n\nAnd yes, please keep the chicken curry set aside and don't eat it until you've heard back. Thanks for your patience, Omar."
  }
